From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: enumerate no instance layers

A program that loads the driver itself, with no Vulkan loader, asks it
for the instance layers too; Mesa's Zink does, and gives up when
vkGetInstanceProcAddr has no vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties. The
loader answers that call itself, so KosmicKrisp never had it. On iOS,
where Zink dlopens KosmicKrisp's framework (0022), it now answers with
no layers.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-opengl-zink-route.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
index 7100d5d..bab4e3f 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
@@ -243,6 +243,17 @@ vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr(VkInstance instance, const char *pName)
    return kk_GetInstanceProcAddr(instance, pName);
 }
 
+/* With no Vulkan loader the program asks the driver itself for the instance
+ * layers (Mesa's Zink does before it creates its instance), and the driver
+ * has none. Through a loader the loader answers and this is not called. */
+VKAPI_ATTR VkResult VKAPI_CALL
+kk_EnumerateInstanceLayerProperties(uint32_t *pPropertyCount,
+                                    VkLayerProperties *pProperties)
+{
+   *pPropertyCount = 0;
+   return VK_SUCCESS;
+}
+
 /* The two entry points a program that loads the driver itself, with no
  * Vulkan loader, looks up by name. Wine's win32u does that on iOS (dlsym of
  * vkGetInstanceProcAddr and vkGetDeviceProcAddr in the library it dlopens),
-- 
